<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Castor and Pollux</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dioscuri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Castor and Pollux, the Dioscuri, were twin heroes and gods of Greek and Roman religion, sons of Leda and, in most accounts, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a>. They were patrons of horsemen and protectors of sailors. Roman legend held that they fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> at the battle of Lake Regillus around 496 BCE and then appeared in the Forum, where a temple was dedicated to them; their cult was strong at nearby Tusculum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/castor-and-pollux.jpg" alt="Castor and Pollux" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castor_Pollux_anagoria.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
